1
00:00:01,735 --> 00:00:05,105
TOUTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

2
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:08,875
This is a technique
using projection mapping,

3
00:00:08,942 --> 00:00:11,244
in which the areas to be cut...

4
00:00:11,311 --> 00:00:13,179
are lit-up and differentiated
by colour.

5
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:16,449
In the case of a tumour,
a unique lighting is...

6
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:19,152
administered before surgery,

7
00:00:19,719 --> 00:00:23,089
and the projection mapping
is shown directly...

8
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:25,458
on the outside of the
internal organs by infrared rays.

9
00:00:31,231 --> 00:00:35,668
Using this technique, even a microscopic
tumour can be recognised.

10
00:00:36,636 --> 00:00:40,206
Then we can keep checking
its position while we remove it.

11
00:00:42,976 --> 00:00:45,812
Even if the internal organs are to move,
the projection is in real-time...

12
00:00:45,979 --> 00:00:47,447
and the accurate position is updated
within 0.1 second.

13
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:48,615
Because of this,
the chances of making a mistake...

14
00:00:48,948 --> 00:00:54,054
during surgery
can be drastically decreased.

15
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:56,790
How much does a machine
like that cost?

16
00:00:57,857 --> 00:00:59,826
Apparently, it's top secret.

17
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:03,063
The world-renowned Dr. Kitano
is so lucky.

18
00:01:03,329 --> 00:01:05,665
He gets the chance to use
the cutting edge technologies.

19
00:01:09,536 --> 00:01:10,670
Where are you going?

20
00:01:11,504 --> 00:01:13,339
It's top secret.

21
00:01:15,775 --> 00:01:18,878
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

22
00:01:21,848 --> 00:01:23,883
- Here you are.
- Great.

23
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:25,018
Thank you.

24
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:37,063
I could just eat him up!

25
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:39,866
Mr. Yuta Yaotome has disappeared

26
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:44,471
from the public and the media
since the day of his last performance.

27
00:01:45,171 --> 00:01:48,408
There are rumours of a secret
ceremony abroad...

28
00:01:48,975 --> 00:01:50,877
Marriage?

29
00:01:50,977 --> 00:01:53,012
- It's nonsense!
- No way!

30
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:54,547
I can't believe it!

31
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:57,383
Yuck. What is wrong with them?
How annoying.

32
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:08,328
You look scary.

33
00:02:08,928 --> 00:02:13,099
<i>In 2016, the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

34
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:15,835
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

35
00:02:16,035 --> 00:02:17,770
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

36
00:02:18,371 --> 00:02:20,907
This case is top secret...

37
00:02:21,074 --> 00:02:23,743
so take care to keep complete
secrecy for the patient.

38
00:02:24,744 --> 00:02:25,578
Yes, ma'am.

39
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,148
In order to prevent others
from entering the room,

40
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:30,183
we have blocked off access
to the elevators.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:31,084
I see.

42
00:02:31,417 --> 00:02:33,219
<i>Famous university hospitals use...</i>

43
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:35,855
<i>their brand power to push into the world.</i>

44
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:39,192
<i>On the other hand,</i>
<i>highly skilled surgeons...</i>

45
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:42,795
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary...</i>

46
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:45,064
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

47
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:46,499
The world of medicine has entered...

48
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:50,770
<i>into the global world</i>
<i>of survival of the fittest.</i>

49
00:02:55,775 --> 00:02:57,377
Thank you very much.

50
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:04,450
<i>In the midst of it,</i>
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>

51
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:07,787
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>
<i>in other words, lone doctors.</i>

52
00:03:08,955 --> 00:03:10,990
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

53
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:15,895
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

54
00:03:16,663 --> 00:03:19,532
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>

55
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:20,833
<i>and the skills she has earned.</i>

56
00:03:22,101 --> 00:03:22,936
What?

57
00:03:23,102 --> 00:03:24,304
OUT OF ORDER

58
00:03:25,305 --> 00:03:26,573
What is this?

59
00:03:34,113 --> 00:03:35,949
It says it's out of order!

60
00:03:36,015 --> 00:03:37,150
But it's working.

61
00:03:38,117 --> 00:03:39,352
Please get out immediately.

62
00:03:39,419 --> 00:03:41,454
I'm in a hurry for an operation.

63
00:03:48,294 --> 00:03:49,662
This is different
from what you promised.

64
00:03:50,096 --> 00:03:53,499
I'll protect the patient's privacy
with all of my power.

65
00:03:56,469 --> 00:03:58,037
A special patient?

66
00:04:00,473 --> 00:04:03,610
Wait, aren't you that person
who was on television earlier?

67
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,645
- What was your name again?
- Stop it.

68
00:04:05,712 --> 00:04:06,546
Daimon.

69
00:04:06,613 --> 00:04:11,217
Dr. Daimon. This is top secret.
You must remain silent.

70
00:04:12,785 --> 00:04:13,786
Yes, ma'am.

71
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:18,291
If I'll keep quiet,
why don't you let me operate?

72
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:20,026
Michiko Daimon!

73
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,308
Let's get started. Scalpel.

74
00:04:44,317 --> 00:04:46,686
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

75
00:04:47,086 --> 00:04:50,189
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

76
00:05:19,585 --> 00:05:21,421
A top secret special patient?

77
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:22,989
Who? Is he famous?

78
00:05:23,256 --> 00:05:25,091
I think so. He was on TV.

79
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:28,027
Hachiman!

80
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:30,129
I'm curious.

81
00:05:30,263 --> 00:05:31,364
What does he look like?

82
00:05:31,531 --> 00:05:34,100
Well, he was wearing sunglasses.

83
00:05:34,233 --> 00:05:36,169
There are many famous people
who wear sunglasses.

84
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:39,238
Michiko, hurry up and pile them.
The rhythm of the game is off.

85
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,840
You've never cared about
the rhythm before.

86
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:42,141
You must have a good hand.

87
00:05:42,375 --> 00:05:43,976
It's top secret.

88
00:05:44,077 --> 00:05:44,911
Yakuman?

89
00:05:44,977 --> 00:05:46,112
It's top secret.

90
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:47,480
Knock on wood!

91
00:05:47,547 --> 00:05:49,148
You might know his name.

92
00:05:49,282 --> 00:05:50,416
Their name?

93
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:51,951
- Eiji Teraoka.
- Who is that?

94
00:05:52,452 --> 00:05:53,886
Ryonosuke Ishikawa.

95
00:05:54,454 --> 00:05:56,589
No, that's not it.

96
00:05:56,723 --> 00:05:58,291
Michiko, I said to get one.

97
00:05:58,424 --> 00:05:59,726
Okay.

98
00:06:00,727 --> 00:06:01,561
Oh!

99
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:08,501
They were saying Mr. Q.

100
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:09,635
Do you mean Mr. Yu?

101
00:06:09,769 --> 00:06:10,670
Yuta Yaotome?

102
00:06:10,803 --> 00:06:11,738
I think that's his name.

103
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:13,239
No way!

104
00:06:13,306 --> 00:06:14,741
If that news went out,
not only the hospital,

105
00:06:14,907 --> 00:06:16,943
but the whole world
would be in panic.

106
00:06:17,009 --> 00:06:19,045
- Is it really that big deal?
- Of course.

107
00:06:19,312 --> 00:06:20,947
He can act and sing and...

108
00:06:21,013 --> 00:06:22,749
is the number one man women

109
00:06:22,815 --> 00:06:23,950
have wanted for five years in a row.

110
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,686
He is a prince
who always wears a veil...

111
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:28,654
in order to hide his privacy.

112
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:31,357
That's gross.

113
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:32,859
- Michiko,
- Yes?

114
00:06:33,025 --> 00:06:35,661
I am relieved.

115
00:06:35,795 --> 00:06:37,663
- What do you mean?
- I win!

116
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:41,467
A double yakuman!

117
00:06:41,534 --> 00:06:43,202
Sushi... Sushi...

118
00:06:43,269 --> 00:06:44,570
I want to eat Sushi!

119
00:06:44,637 --> 00:06:46,439
Forget about the Sushi.

120
00:06:46,506 --> 00:06:47,707
What illness does Mr. Yu have?

121
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:51,344
Not sure. Isn't this amazing?

122
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:53,880
Liver cancer, stage 4a.

123
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:57,183
There are several tumours
spreading from the right side...

124
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:01,287
of your liver,
to the left over a vast area.

125
00:07:06,793 --> 00:07:09,862
So it is pretty serious, isn't it?

126
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:11,564
Don't worry.

127
00:07:13,366 --> 00:07:14,700
You can remove the tumours, right?

128
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:17,470
If you leave it to me,
it is possible.

129
00:07:18,571 --> 00:07:21,107
Thank you in advance.

130
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:23,342
Please do not worry about privacy.

131
00:07:23,509 --> 00:07:24,911
We will not leak this information.

132
00:07:24,977 --> 00:07:25,878
Never.

133
00:07:26,379 --> 00:07:28,981
Kitano, you, too.

134
00:07:29,248 --> 00:07:31,684
I have no interest in who he is.

135
00:07:32,151 --> 00:07:36,122
All I want to do is to remove cancer
from my patient. That is all I want.

136
00:07:49,602 --> 00:07:50,470
Kitano!

137
00:07:50,903 --> 00:07:52,772
Hold on! Kitano!

138
00:07:54,073 --> 00:07:55,041
What is it?

139
00:07:56,175 --> 00:08:00,012
Do you... not realise
who that patient is?

140
00:08:02,682 --> 00:08:04,584
He is such a VIP that

141
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:08,187
if it were leaked that he is here,
Japan would topple over.

142
00:08:10,122 --> 00:08:12,191
I know you're worried about...

143
00:08:12,291 --> 00:08:13,860
getting into trouble
with Director Hiruma...

144
00:08:13,926 --> 00:08:16,762
because you'll be in trouble, too.

145
00:08:16,929 --> 00:08:18,998
- Huh?
- Set your mind at ease.

146
00:08:19,232 --> 00:08:22,401
I will complete
this operation perfectly.

147
00:08:24,203 --> 00:08:27,273
Or, would you like to perform it?

148
00:08:28,975 --> 00:08:30,276
Who do you think you're talking to?

149
00:08:30,409 --> 00:08:34,146
I need to prepare for a conference,
so please excuse me.

150
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:43,689
DO NOT LEAK TO THE PUBLIC.

151
00:08:46,792 --> 00:08:48,794
SURGICAL CONFERENCE

152
00:08:49,929 --> 00:08:51,697
The patient in this case...

153
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,635
is top secret.

154
00:08:57,470 --> 00:09:00,473
This means that you must not say
a word about the details discussed

155
00:09:01,307 --> 00:09:04,644
in this conference.
Do you understand?

156
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:06,979
Yes sir.

157
00:09:09,982 --> 00:09:12,785
As for the patient's name,

158
00:09:12,985 --> 00:09:14,554
we will create an alias
and call him...

159
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,989
DO NOT LEAK TO THE PUBLIC.

160
00:09:18,424 --> 00:09:19,492
Mr. Johnson.

161
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:20,560
Is he a foreigner?

162
00:09:21,794 --> 00:09:24,463
No. Mr. Johnson is Japanese.

163
00:09:24,597 --> 00:09:26,265
Then why don't you call him
Mr. Sato or Mr. Suzuki?

164
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:28,301
- Mr. Johnson...
- Are you ignoring me?

165
00:09:28,768 --> 00:09:30,803
has liver cancer, stage 4a.

166
00:09:31,203 --> 00:09:34,307
The main tumour is on the right
side and is 13 centimetres,

167
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:38,077
and there are also tumours
in S1, S4, and S3.

168
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,780
The tumours are shown clearly here.

169
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:42,949
We must remove them closely...

170
00:09:43,015 --> 00:09:45,084
to the boundaries and leave at least
20 percent of the liver intact.

171
00:09:45,384 --> 00:09:48,254
Or the liver will be unable to
function properly,

172
00:09:48,321 --> 00:09:50,623
it's highly likely that he'll suffer
liver failure.

173
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:53,859
Having said that,
if even a slight bit of tumour...

174
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:55,595
is left behind,
the tumour will grow again.

175
00:09:55,861 --> 00:09:58,497
We must remove
the tumours completely...

176
00:09:58,564 --> 00:10:00,566
and it is an exceedingly
difficult operation.

177
00:10:01,834 --> 00:10:03,502
How about minimising the tumours?

178
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,539
After doing so,
it is easier to operate.

179
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:07,940
That's a good idea.

180
00:10:08,207 --> 00:10:09,575
There is also a better chance
to remove it all...

181
00:10:09,642 --> 00:10:12,511
making it harder to come back and...

182
00:10:12,578 --> 00:10:15,848
Mr. Johnson wants to be treated
in a short period of time.

183
00:10:15,982 --> 00:10:18,017
Is Mr. Johnson busy?

184
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:19,785
Mr. Johnson is very busy.

185
00:10:19,885 --> 00:10:22,722
He may be the busiest man in Japan.

186
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:25,725
- That's incredible.
- Mr. Johnson is amazing.

187
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:28,327
Stop saying Mr. Johnson!
Mr. Johnson. Mr. Johnson...

188
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:30,763
Well... We do not have much time.

189
00:10:32,231 --> 00:10:34,000
So we cannot do
a chemical treatment.

190
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:37,470
With that said, I will be using
the projection mapping system.

191
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,740
I'll show you a demonstration...

192
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:43,376
to perform a perfect operation.

193
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:47,279
I want to do it.

194
00:10:49,248 --> 00:10:50,950
This is an operation
using the latest technology,

195
00:10:51,017 --> 00:10:53,386
and there is only
one machine in New York.

196
00:10:53,619 --> 00:10:54,720
You don't have
any experience, right?

197
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:55,955
So let me try.

198
00:10:56,088 --> 00:10:59,492
Are you dumb? Didn't I just say
it is a brand new machine?

199
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:03,029
In order to use it, you need
the latest skill and sense.

200
00:11:03,095 --> 00:11:06,432
That is correct. Mr. Johnson is the
most special patient we can have.

201
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:08,300
Not a single mistake will be forgiven.

202
00:11:08,567 --> 00:11:10,703
Johnson, Johnson...

203
00:11:10,936 --> 00:11:12,304
How about you just call him
by his real name?

204
00:11:12,571 --> 00:11:15,374
Yaotome... what was it again?

205
00:11:19,612 --> 00:11:20,813
Yaotome something?

206
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,182
Mr. Yu?

207
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:25,484
If I can't operate, I'm going home.

208
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:27,219
Daimon!

209
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,555
Daimon! It's absolute secrecy!

210
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:31,023
- No way.
- Yuta Yaotome?

211
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:35,494
Mr. Yu!

212
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:37,797
Don't say a word!

213
00:11:38,264 --> 00:11:39,532
Please do not worry.

214
00:11:40,299 --> 00:11:42,601
This hospital's surgical team
is the best in Japan.

215
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:48,808
Please leave everything to me...
and get some rest for today.

216
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:10,362
Hey, who is the special patient?

217
00:12:11,964 --> 00:12:15,568
What? You didn't hear?

218
00:12:15,634 --> 00:12:16,569
Don't play dumb.

219
00:12:16,902 --> 00:12:18,571
That's strange.

220
00:12:18,938 --> 00:12:23,242
Well, I'm sure there was just some kind of
mistake while transmitting the message.

221
00:12:28,848 --> 00:12:30,282
Right? It's top secret.

222
00:12:30,716 --> 00:12:33,219
I was told to take care of
the hospital...

223
00:12:33,552 --> 00:12:35,688
while Director Hiruma is in London
for an academic meeting.

224
00:12:35,888 --> 00:12:37,423
There is no reason
I shouldn't know about this.

225
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:40,493
That's strange...
I heard about it.

226
00:12:41,026 --> 00:12:41,927
Well...

227
00:12:44,964 --> 00:12:48,134
I'm sorry. It's a secret.

228
00:12:53,339 --> 00:12:55,775
The surgical department
didn't leak any information.

229
00:12:56,175 --> 00:12:58,778
That's impossible. Ask again!

230
00:12:59,512 --> 00:13:00,346
Yes sir.

231
00:13:09,221 --> 00:13:12,424
- Chief, about the year-end party,
- Okay.

232
00:13:12,825 --> 00:13:14,426
is the same pub and course...

233
00:13:14,493 --> 00:13:16,262
as always, okay?

234
00:13:16,829 --> 00:13:18,998
Or how about...

235
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:21,200
we have a luxurious course meal?

236
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,468
How difference is the price?

237
00:13:22,835 --> 00:13:23,869
20 dollars.

238
00:13:25,171 --> 00:13:27,273
We will have the usual one.

239
00:13:27,439 --> 00:13:28,274
Yes sir.

240
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:37,249
YOU HAVE A NEW MAIL

241
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:40,319
CONFIDENTIAL

242
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:42,021
UNLOCK AND OPEN

243
00:13:42,354 --> 00:13:43,722
SECRET DELIVERY COMPLETED.

244
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:45,424
SECRET DELIVERY

245
00:13:45,958 --> 00:13:47,760
Secret delivery?

246
00:13:59,271 --> 00:14:00,906
Where did everyone go?

247
00:14:02,308 --> 00:14:03,342
Secret activities?

248
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:12,818
FROM: KIKAWADA
TITLE: SECRET DELIVERY NOTIFICATION

249
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,131
This elevator...

250
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:27,499
is for everyone.

251
00:14:34,673 --> 00:14:37,009
Are you a fan of Yuta Yaotome?

252
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:38,978
Huh?

253
00:14:39,645 --> 00:14:42,982
That's why you keep ambushing him.
Every single day.

254
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:47,253
Never.
However, I am interested.

255
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:48,721
What?

256
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:50,222
In your operation.

257
00:14:51,957 --> 00:14:55,427
Let me do it. I never fail.

258
00:15:05,771 --> 00:15:06,672
Here you go.

259
00:15:13,312 --> 00:15:14,280
Sit down.

260
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:15,214
Huh?

261
00:15:15,514 --> 00:15:16,682
Sit down, please.

262
00:15:18,183 --> 00:15:19,051
Yes sir.

263
00:15:35,234 --> 00:15:36,068
Oops, I saw you.

264
00:15:38,537 --> 00:15:41,674
Is it okay for you to sit there?

265
00:15:44,009 --> 00:15:48,347
This is a secret between
just the two of us.

266
00:15:51,517 --> 00:15:53,819
I don't know
if I can keep it to myself.

267
00:15:55,821 --> 00:15:58,557
There's a price, Dr. Saionji.

268
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:06,131
Okay, then how about...
I tell you another secret.

269
00:16:06,598 --> 00:16:07,833
Then, will you forgive me?

270
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:08,767
A secret?

271
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,137
Tell me.

272
00:16:13,205 --> 00:16:14,606
By sharing a secret,

273
00:16:17,543 --> 00:16:18,644
our love grows.

274
00:16:30,923 --> 00:16:31,790
Ouch!

275
00:16:32,057 --> 00:16:34,126
Yaotome? Yuta?

276
00:16:35,027 --> 00:16:37,629
Using this projection mapping,

277
00:16:37,696 --> 00:16:40,632
I will accurately remove
all of the cancerous tumours.

278
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:45,304
However, there is the possibility
of complications such as...

279
00:16:45,371 --> 00:16:47,873
liver failure or haemorrhage
during operation.

280
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:51,377
Do you mean he could die
during surgery?

281
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,245
There's a possibility.

282
00:16:53,779 --> 00:17:00,753
Mr. Yaotome.
We're just informing you of risks...

283
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,921
and every single possible cases.

284
00:17:02,988 --> 00:17:04,656
If we do not operate,
you have six months at best.

285
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,959
I am the only one
who can do this surgery.

286
00:17:07,092 --> 00:17:08,994
In other words, there is
no other choice.

287
00:17:10,763 --> 00:17:12,164
Please sign this form.

288
00:17:17,836 --> 00:17:19,405
SURGERY CONSENT FORM

289
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:33,652
It's true!

290
00:17:33,786 --> 00:17:35,087
Mr. Yu!

291
00:17:49,168 --> 00:17:51,170
Mr. Yu is hospitalised here!

292
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:52,404
Why is he here?

293
00:17:52,504 --> 00:17:53,672
What floor is he on?

294
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,940
I love him.

295
00:17:55,007 --> 00:17:56,141
Out of the way!

296
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:57,776
What on earth is going on?

297
00:18:04,016 --> 00:18:05,884
THIS FILE CANNOT BE OPENED.

298
00:18:05,951 --> 00:18:06,785
Gosh.

299
00:18:12,157 --> 00:18:14,793
What? Why can't I open the file?

300
00:18:18,397 --> 00:18:19,798
Did someone use my computer?

301
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,101
I didn't.

302
00:18:22,634 --> 00:18:25,003
- I didn't use it, either.
- Me, either.

303
00:18:25,137 --> 00:18:27,473
It's weird.
It worked well yesterday.

304
00:18:29,174 --> 00:18:30,742
I won't be mad, so just be honest.

305
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,411
Who was it?

306
00:18:33,579 --> 00:18:34,947
Nobody touched it?

307
00:18:36,081 --> 00:18:36,982
Chief Kikawada.

308
00:18:37,483 --> 00:18:39,585
There's an error message...
Someone must have used it.

309
00:18:39,685 --> 00:18:40,719
There's something more important.

310
00:18:43,322 --> 00:18:45,057
Yuta Yaotome is secretly
being hospitalised?

311
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:47,025
Did you really not know...

312
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,027
about such an important
secret matter?

313
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:49,962
No.

314
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,397
Seriously?

315
00:18:52,831 --> 00:18:54,399
We will move to another hospital.

316
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:55,934
We cannot stay here any longer.

317
00:18:56,268 --> 00:18:57,636
Please wait.

318
00:18:57,769 --> 00:19:00,806
You promised over and over
to protect his privacy.

319
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:03,642
How could something
like this happen?

320
00:19:03,709 --> 00:19:05,511
What is this?

321
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,279
How did this happen?

322
00:19:07,346 --> 00:19:08,447
MR. YU IS IN THE HOSIPITAL!

323
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:11,083
There must be a mistake!
Please calm down.

324
00:19:11,216 --> 00:19:14,253
How could I calm down
in a situation like this?

325
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,622
We understand the mistake
we have made.

326
00:19:16,688 --> 00:19:19,191
But it is not wise to transfer
to another hospital right now.

327
00:19:19,258 --> 00:19:22,528
Since everyone knows...
he's staying here,

328
00:19:22,961 --> 00:19:24,830
it's more dangerous for him
to be here.

329
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:26,431
Let's go.

330
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:30,302
How on earth did this happen?

331
00:19:31,737 --> 00:19:35,841
Mr. Yuta Yaotome, please come back.
It's dangerous outside!

332
00:19:35,908 --> 00:19:36,909
Come back to the room.

333
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:40,779
That's enough.
Nothing you say will change my mind!

334
00:19:41,647 --> 00:19:42,848
Excuse me.

335
00:19:42,915 --> 00:19:43,882
Please wait.

336
00:19:45,284 --> 00:19:46,251
Daimon!

337
00:19:50,923 --> 00:19:52,524
You're not going to
have the surgery?

338
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:55,627
No.

339
00:19:57,729 --> 00:20:00,032
If you leave now,
you're going to die.

340
00:20:13,946 --> 00:20:14,913
There he is!

341
00:20:15,147 --> 00:20:18,050
Mr. Yu!

342
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:21,119
- Please show your face!
- Please spare us a minute.

343
00:20:25,691 --> 00:20:27,192
Mr. Yaotome!
What is your illness?

344
00:20:27,259 --> 00:20:28,393
Mr. Yu!

345
00:20:31,129 --> 00:20:33,165
Get out of the way.

346
00:20:33,432 --> 00:20:34,933
Are you his fiancée?

347
00:20:35,033 --> 00:20:36,201
A woman doctor?

348
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:37,569
What is your name?

349
00:20:38,537 --> 00:20:40,339
- Just one minute.
- Please.

350
00:20:40,806 --> 00:20:42,941
Mr. Yaotome?

351
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:44,509
Mr. Yaotome! Are you okay?

352
00:20:44,676 --> 00:20:46,178
Mr. Yaotome!

353
00:20:46,278 --> 00:20:47,312
Move!

354
00:20:47,379 --> 00:20:51,183
- Mr. Yaotome!
- Is he okay?

355
00:20:54,019 --> 00:20:56,989
Advanced liver impairment.
Someone bring a stretcher!

356
00:20:58,991 --> 00:21:00,926
LIVER PROTECTION DRUG

357
00:21:10,168 --> 00:21:11,069
Where am I?

358
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:12,671
The hospital room.

359
00:21:13,405 --> 00:21:15,607
Your liver function decreased
and you lost consciousness.

360
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,849
- Get the discharge papers ready.
- Okay

361
00:21:23,915 --> 00:21:25,183
What are you saying?

362
00:21:25,317 --> 00:21:27,986
This man... is a star.

363
00:21:28,553 --> 00:21:29,388
So what?

364
00:21:30,822 --> 00:21:35,627
To the people, there is no such
thing as a sick Yuta Yaotome.

365
00:21:35,894 --> 00:21:36,762
Huh?

366
00:21:38,330 --> 00:21:43,902
No matter what happens, I have to be the
Yuta Yaotome that everyone longs for.

367
00:21:46,872 --> 00:21:50,575
I must be a radiant and
grant-wishing presence all the time.

368
00:21:53,512 --> 00:21:54,680
How annoying.

369
00:21:58,083 --> 00:21:59,418
You're so conceited.

370
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,588
You may be a star or whatever,

371
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:07,459
but I don't think the world cares about
you as much as you think they do.

372
00:22:08,293 --> 00:22:11,296
I had no idea who you were.

373
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:17,102
Right now, you are not a star.
You are just a patient.

374
00:22:18,103 --> 00:22:19,037
How dare you!

375
00:22:20,305 --> 00:22:24,476
If he wants to die...
as the annoying Yuta Yaotome,

376
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,244
that's a different story.

377
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:44,463
How did the news about
Yuta Yaotome leak?

378
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:46,365
We are currently investigating.

379
00:22:47,399 --> 00:22:51,436
What are you... even here for?

380
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:54,106
What happened to full
information management?

381
00:22:54,673 --> 00:22:55,907
I'm very sorry.

382
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:59,878
I pay... good money for you.

383
00:23:00,078 --> 00:23:04,850
Not being able to protect the privacy
of patients is out of the question!

384
00:23:05,917 --> 00:23:08,553
I'll take full responsibility.

385
00:23:09,154 --> 00:23:14,659
Your plan to increase the publicity
of the hospital has failed.

386
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,828
That's what I will see this as.

387
00:23:22,601 --> 00:23:26,071
I apologise for this clumsy mistake
from the bottom of my heart.

388
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:28,573
However,

389
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:29,908
Please do the surgery.

390
00:23:30,776 --> 00:23:31,610
Huh?

391
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:34,346
I have decided to get the treatment.

392
00:23:36,615 --> 00:23:37,783
I understand.

393
00:23:38,383 --> 00:23:39,985
You can count on me.

394
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,119
However,

395
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:45,157
we would like you to be even more thorough
with our privacy from here on out.

396
00:23:45,357 --> 00:23:46,291
Of course.

397
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:52,697
Hey. I heard you picked
a fight with Yuta Yaotome.

398
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:54,299
A fight?

399
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:56,902
Did you call him conceited?

400
00:23:58,637 --> 00:24:00,939
Aren't all stars conceited?

401
00:24:01,406 --> 00:24:04,409
Don't make it any rockier than this.

402
00:24:04,810 --> 00:24:09,247
Daimon.
Yaotome agreed to get my operation.

403
00:24:10,415 --> 00:24:12,951
- Is that so?
- I hope you will be able to observe it.

404
00:24:14,319 --> 00:24:16,721
This will be the very first case in Japan.

405
00:24:17,322 --> 00:24:19,624
There is surely something
for you to learn.

406
00:24:26,865 --> 00:24:30,135
Our superstar... is conceited, too!

407
00:24:34,005 --> 00:24:36,141
It's five so I'm going home!

408
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:41,379
Is that conceited, too?

409
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,482
No. That's just called being selfish.

410
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:44,416
I see.

411
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:49,754
Huh?

412
00:24:52,958 --> 00:24:54,626
I'm coming.

413
00:24:57,229 --> 00:24:58,463
Top secret?

414
00:24:59,231 --> 00:25:01,266
It's from Chief Kikawada.
I wonder what it could be.

415
00:25:03,268 --> 00:25:05,470
- I got it, too.
- Huh?

416
00:25:05,537 --> 00:25:06,738
Me, too.

417
00:25:06,905 --> 00:25:10,509
- Me, too.
- I got it, too.

418
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:12,344
How is this top secret?

419
00:25:13,778 --> 00:25:15,447
UNLOCK AND OPEN

420
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:19,851
DELIVERY COMPLETED.

421
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:54,986
HELLO, EVERYONE
PLEASE CHECK THE ATTACHED FILE.

422
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:57,422
CONFIDENTIAL

423
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:04,462
I am honoured to assist you
on this surgery.

424
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:07,832
I would like the younger generation
to see cutting-edge surgery, too.

425
00:26:08,466 --> 00:26:09,634
Is the preparation
for the transfusion complete?

426
00:26:09,701 --> 00:26:10,835
Yes, it's ready.

427
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:11,736
Okay.

428
00:26:20,679 --> 00:26:22,347
Are you controlling information?

429
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,315
Yes.

430
00:26:26,351 --> 00:26:29,354
Dr. Daimon. Why are you here?

431
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,989
I'm here to observe.

432
00:26:31,556 --> 00:26:33,925
Are you finally interested in
studying the latest technology?

433
00:26:42,133 --> 00:26:43,101
Okay, guys.

434
00:26:43,168 --> 00:26:46,271
We will now begin dissecting
the liver into thirds for removal,

435
00:26:46,338 --> 00:26:48,640
also known as a S3
sectional ablation.

436
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:50,342
Let's do our best.

437
00:26:50,408 --> 00:26:51,543
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

438
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:56,247
Vitals are 124 and 83.
Heart rate is 68. Sinus.

439
00:26:56,314 --> 00:26:57,215
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

440
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,251
Incision.

441
00:27:07,892 --> 00:27:09,327
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

442
00:27:20,572 --> 00:27:22,741
SURGERY HOUR

443
00:27:30,382 --> 00:27:34,619
Now, we will project the
projection mapping image.

444
00:27:50,602 --> 00:27:51,469
PROJECTION HAS BEGUN

445
00:27:57,742 --> 00:27:59,110
Watch closely.

446
00:27:59,911 --> 00:28:01,179
It's amazing.

447
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:05,583
We will cut parallel to this
boundary line.

448
00:28:05,917 --> 00:28:07,919
First, I will incise the area three.

449
00:28:08,019 --> 00:28:09,387
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

450
00:28:24,235 --> 00:28:25,070
CANNOT BE OPENED

451
00:28:25,770 --> 00:28:29,808
The cause of the error
is a computer virus.

452
00:28:30,075 --> 00:28:30,942
What?

453
00:28:31,276 --> 00:28:33,044
Why is there something like that
on my computer?

454
00:28:33,178 --> 00:28:34,946
Did you open any strange e-mails?

455
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:36,548
I don't think so.

456
00:28:37,082 --> 00:28:39,751
Hey, system engineer. Hurry it up!

457
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:41,753
The Internal Medicine Department's
computers are off, too.

458
00:28:41,820 --> 00:28:43,455
- Really?
- Yeah.

459
00:28:43,521 --> 00:28:46,424
Chief, did you open
any strange e-mails?

460
00:28:47,325 --> 00:28:48,593
- Strange e-mails?
- Yes.

461
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:52,030
YOU'VE GOT A NEW MESSAGE

462
00:28:53,364 --> 00:28:54,466
UNLOCK AND OPEN

463
00:28:54,766 --> 00:28:56,167
DELIVERY COMPLETED

464
00:28:56,768 --> 00:28:58,470
Secret delivery?

465
00:29:01,172 --> 00:29:02,073
I don't think so.

466
00:29:03,675 --> 00:29:07,245
If you look at the inbox, can you tell
which e-mail is the source of infection?

467
00:29:07,312 --> 00:29:08,146
- Yes.
- What?

468
00:29:09,514 --> 00:29:10,849
Stop!

469
00:29:11,916 --> 00:29:13,051
- What's wrong?
- That's not good.

470
00:29:13,151 --> 00:29:14,152
Why not?

471
00:29:14,886 --> 00:29:16,488
- I don't think it's good.
- Why not?

472
00:29:16,554 --> 00:29:18,690
- Shut it, Glasses!
- You have glasses on, too!

473
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:20,158
Please check.

474
00:29:22,026 --> 00:29:23,128
Here it is.

475
00:29:23,928 --> 00:29:25,830
A secret delivery e-mail.

476
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:26,798
A secret delivery?

477
00:29:26,865 --> 00:29:28,633
Kikawada.

478
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,135
Glasses.

479
00:29:31,803 --> 00:29:32,771
I'm sorry.

480
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:54,793
What's wrong?

481
00:29:56,427 --> 00:29:57,262
There is an error.

482
00:29:57,395 --> 00:29:59,731
Error? What do you mean?

483
00:29:59,864 --> 00:30:02,200
Doctor! We got an error over here, too!

484
00:30:02,934 --> 00:30:03,768
You idiots.

485
00:30:03,902 --> 00:30:05,837
What did you touch?

486
00:30:12,677 --> 00:30:17,215
Chief Kikawada. Do you have
Dr. Kitano's e-mail address?

487
00:30:17,682 --> 00:30:18,616
What if I do?

488
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:22,053
Hey, has the superstar's
operation already started?

489
00:30:23,354 --> 00:30:24,289
For quite some time.

490
00:30:29,961 --> 00:30:31,062
Why does that matter?

491
00:30:32,263 --> 00:30:33,898
This is horrible.

492
00:30:35,433 --> 00:30:36,467
Dr. Kitano!

493
00:30:36,868 --> 00:30:38,636
Contact the information branch.

494
00:30:38,703 --> 00:30:39,571
Yes, sir.

495
00:30:41,372 --> 00:30:43,908
What is happening?

496
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:51,149
What is going on?

497
00:30:53,551 --> 00:30:54,519
Excuse me.

498
00:30:54,886 --> 00:30:58,990
Dr. Kitano! There is a possibility
that your computer is infected.

499
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:01,092
- What?
- What?

500
00:31:11,169 --> 00:31:13,037
We cannot operate with this.

501
00:31:14,005 --> 00:31:14,939
Dr. Kitano.

502
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,042
SURGERY HOUR

503
00:31:24,115 --> 00:31:25,016
It's inoperable.

504
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:33,391
It's inoperable.

505
00:31:37,195 --> 00:31:38,229
Don't close.

506
00:31:40,064 --> 00:31:42,433
You can't just declare it
as inoperable now.

507
00:31:42,533 --> 00:31:45,570
How will you remove the tumours
without the projection mapping?

508
00:31:45,637 --> 00:31:46,638
I can do it.

509
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:50,275
If you don't leave more than
20 percent of the liver,

510
00:31:50,341 --> 00:31:52,443
it will cost him his life!

511
00:31:52,777 --> 00:31:55,013
I will leave the liver.

512
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:57,181
- Surgical light.
- Here you are.

513
00:31:58,950 --> 00:32:00,218
There is a lot of bleeding.

514
00:32:00,318 --> 00:32:01,753
How long do you plan
to leave him open?

515
00:32:02,020 --> 00:32:03,855
All that has stopped is the
mapping machine, right?

516
00:32:04,222 --> 00:32:05,056
This one is okay.

517
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:07,558
This is my operation.
I do not give you permission.

518
00:32:07,792 --> 00:32:10,495
You can't do it
without that machine.

519
00:32:12,230 --> 00:32:14,666
Help him!

520
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:18,236
I don't care who it is,
just save Mr. Yu!

521
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:21,673
Mr. Yu! Hang in there!

522
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:26,511
Is she...

523
00:32:27,312 --> 00:32:28,379
a fan of his?

524
00:32:28,546 --> 00:32:29,981
Don't be stupid.

525
00:32:30,682 --> 00:32:33,184
Look at her, does she look like a fan?

526
00:32:33,551 --> 00:32:34,552
Oh, she's an aficionado?

527
00:32:34,919 --> 00:32:35,920
No!

528
00:32:37,021 --> 00:32:38,423
For someone of her age,

529
00:32:39,123 --> 00:32:40,224
you call that a groupie.

530
00:32:40,325 --> 00:32:41,392
Who cares about this.

531
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:47,665
Michiko Daimon! You never fail!

532
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:49,100
What are his vitals?

533
00:32:49,167 --> 00:32:51,936
Blood pressure is 115 and 77.
Heart rate is 76.

534
00:32:52,870 --> 00:32:54,939
I am going to continue
with the area three dissection.

535
00:32:55,039 --> 00:32:55,873
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here you are.

536
00:33:10,188 --> 00:33:11,122
Excuse me.

537
00:33:11,522 --> 00:33:13,758
Daimon, stop.
There is no projection mapping.

538
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,759
You're being reckless!

539
00:33:16,394 --> 00:33:19,764
I never fail, even without a map.

540
00:33:23,835 --> 00:33:25,103
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

541
00:33:34,645 --> 00:33:39,417
Did she memorise...
the locations of each tumour?

542
00:33:39,550 --> 00:33:41,185
That's a piece of cake.

543
00:33:42,253 --> 00:33:46,424
Don't just stand there.
Ligate the blood vessels.

544
00:33:51,162 --> 00:33:52,864
- 30 suture.
- Here you are.

545
00:34:08,146 --> 00:34:11,282
SURGERY HOUR

546
00:34:16,687 --> 00:34:18,056
The area three has been removed.

547
00:34:18,156 --> 00:34:19,624
I will now begin with
the S3 separation.

548
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,392
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

549
00:34:21,659 --> 00:34:23,828
- Lower my loupes.
- Yes ma'am. Excuse me.

550
00:34:33,671 --> 00:34:36,674
Wow. She's cutting it
very precisely.

551
00:34:54,058 --> 00:34:55,493
Done. What are his vitals?

552
00:34:55,560 --> 00:34:59,197
Blood pressure is 109 and 74.
Heart rate is 70. Sinus.

553
00:35:07,338 --> 00:35:09,474
You can be everyone's star again.

554
00:35:09,941 --> 00:35:12,043
- Good work.
- Good work.

555
00:35:14,378 --> 00:35:15,913
Bravo!

556
00:35:16,347 --> 00:35:19,150
Dr. Daimon! Bravo!

557
00:35:19,717 --> 00:35:22,987
Michiko Daimon! Bravo!
That was wonderful!

558
00:35:48,779 --> 00:35:50,615
That was a splendid operation.

559
00:35:51,883 --> 00:35:52,917
Thanks.

560
00:35:54,519 --> 00:35:55,586
With that said,

561
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:58,623
your operation is a gamble.
One day you will reach your limits.

562
00:36:00,925 --> 00:36:04,495
Our job is to protect patients'
lives while avoiding risks.

563
00:36:04,562 --> 00:36:06,497
That is why the latest technology
is necessary.

564
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:11,602
I don't get it.

565
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:18,576
You were looking at the monitor
frantically when it shut off.

566
00:36:18,676 --> 00:36:21,779
Why don't you look at
the patient right in front of you?

567
00:36:25,116 --> 00:36:29,253
Isn't it a surgeon's job to see with
our eyes and cut with our hands?

568
00:36:46,337 --> 00:36:48,739
TOUTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

569
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:53,044
I told you not to carelessly
open virus e-mails!

570
00:36:54,645 --> 00:36:56,414
How clumsy.

571
00:36:56,647 --> 00:36:57,481
You're fired!

572
00:36:58,249 --> 00:36:59,083
Please forgive me.

573
00:36:59,317 --> 00:37:00,685
You, too.

574
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:02,587
It's your fault.

575
00:37:03,020 --> 00:37:05,957
You failed to manage
information properly!

576
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:07,291
Huh?

577
00:37:09,193 --> 00:37:10,361
Do you think so?

578
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:15,666
Deputy Director.

579
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:20,671
In director Hiruma's absence,

580
00:37:20,738 --> 00:37:22,640
you accepted a patient
with great risks.

581
00:37:24,141 --> 00:37:27,245
That is because you are
a big fan of Yuta Yaotome's.

582
00:37:28,813 --> 00:37:30,448
In other words, you're childish.

583
00:37:31,549 --> 00:37:34,085
I'm fed up with you praising him!

584
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:39,423
Hey.

585
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:42,593
Are you laughing?

586
00:37:43,661 --> 00:37:46,063
The leak to the media
was not a virus,

587
00:37:46,597 --> 00:37:48,266
but spread over social media.

588
00:37:49,667 --> 00:37:51,602
The source of information
was Shiromizu.

589
00:37:52,536 --> 00:37:55,172
The private secretary of Director.

590
00:37:57,642 --> 00:37:59,043
Oh, really?

591
00:38:00,011 --> 00:38:03,114
We have already investigated.
You leaked it to her!

592
00:38:03,347 --> 00:38:04,181
- Huh?
- What?

593
00:38:04,582 --> 00:38:06,183
- I didn't.
- Dr. Saionji!

594
00:38:06,250 --> 00:38:08,686
While Director Hiruma
was out, what did you do to her?

595
00:38:08,819 --> 00:38:10,187
No, no...

596
00:38:10,354 --> 00:38:12,390
- Is that so?
- Huh?

597
00:38:12,757 --> 00:38:14,659
If you don't want me to come in,

598
00:38:15,159 --> 00:38:17,128
you need to lock the door.

599
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:20,231
Important information may be leaked.

600
00:38:21,098 --> 00:38:22,300
Here is the melon.

601
00:38:23,734 --> 00:38:25,202
Here is the bill.

602
00:38:31,742 --> 00:38:32,576
What?

603
00:38:33,144 --> 00:38:36,080
We can't pay this huge amount.

604
00:38:36,213 --> 00:38:37,281
Excuse me.

605
00:38:38,616 --> 00:38:41,118
This is an unreasonable bill.
Please look it over again.

606
00:38:41,552 --> 00:38:42,753
Is that so?

607
00:38:43,854 --> 00:38:46,624
Deputy Director Kubo accepts patients

608
00:38:46,691 --> 00:38:49,160
based on personal feelings.

609
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:54,932
Chief Kikawada carelessly...
infected computers with viruses...

610
00:38:54,999 --> 00:38:57,468
and puts patients' lives in danger.

611
00:38:58,402 --> 00:39:02,139
Dr. Saionji...
hit on Director's secretary and...

612
00:39:02,506 --> 00:39:06,877
revealed top secret... to her in bed.

613
00:39:06,944 --> 00:39:09,080
It wasn't a bed, though.

614
00:39:09,313 --> 00:39:10,815
Is that a threat?

615
00:39:11,482 --> 00:39:13,351
Take it as you like.

616
00:39:15,086 --> 00:39:16,554
We'll pay it.

617
00:39:17,955 --> 00:39:19,690
Thank you very much.

618
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,128
Michiko! Yes!

619
00:39:28,699 --> 00:39:29,667
There is no problem.

620
00:39:31,869 --> 00:39:35,873
Thank you. It wasn't too bad
being just another patient.

621
00:39:40,511 --> 00:39:41,812
Daihachi Yamada.

622
00:39:42,446 --> 00:39:43,547
Huh?

623
00:39:44,281 --> 00:39:45,483
It's my real name.

624
00:39:46,083 --> 00:39:47,184
Seriously?

625
00:39:49,854 --> 00:39:54,725
From now on, I'll try to live as
Daihachi Yamada every once in a while.

626
00:39:56,494 --> 00:39:57,928
That sounds good.

627
00:40:04,001 --> 00:40:05,136
Daihachi?

628
00:40:08,339 --> 00:40:10,808
We here at
Toutei University hospital,

629
00:40:11,375 --> 00:40:15,479
with superior technological strength,
and prominent surgeons,

630
00:40:15,813 --> 00:40:21,719
have successfully completed...
the operation... on a national star.

631
00:40:23,854 --> 00:40:26,957
Yuta Yaotome. Please rest assured.

632
00:40:27,591 --> 00:40:32,463
Our Yuta Yaotome... has come back.

633
00:40:32,563 --> 00:40:35,099
Yuta Yaotome, please come in!

634
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,467
What?

635
00:40:40,538 --> 00:40:41,505
This is unbelievable.

636
00:40:49,079 --> 00:40:50,014
Thank you.

637
00:40:55,719 --> 00:40:56,754
That's enough.

638
00:41:02,226 --> 00:41:08,032
Today, I'm here to apologise...
for making you worried.

639
00:41:10,100 --> 00:41:11,702
Why is someone who hates cameras

640
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:13,804
having an interview like this?

641
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:19,743
Until now, I always hid who I truly am.

642
00:41:21,679 --> 00:41:23,447
But when I was sick, I realised...

643
00:41:25,182 --> 00:41:26,784
there is no such thing
as a perfect person.

644
00:41:28,252 --> 00:41:33,023
That is why I would like everyone to
see me, Yuta Yaotome, just the way I am.

645
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:37,761
I would be happy if you
could continue to support me.

646
00:41:45,936 --> 00:41:46,971
Thus,

647
00:41:48,305 --> 00:41:53,777
I would like to thank
Toutei University Hospital...

648
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:56,113
from the bottom of my heart...
for giving me another chance to live.

649
00:41:57,948 --> 00:41:59,216
Thank you very much.

650
00:42:03,954 --> 00:42:07,591
Lastly, I have an announcement
to make to everyone.

651
00:42:10,060 --> 00:42:11,962
I, Yuta Yaotome...

652
00:42:13,430 --> 00:42:14,698
Come here.

653
00:42:17,935 --> 00:42:21,205
I married my manager,
Yumi Kawai today.

654
00:42:29,713 --> 00:42:32,783
Please continue to give
your warm support.

655
00:42:34,285 --> 00:42:35,920
My Mr. Yu.

656
00:42:36,353 --> 00:42:39,056
My Mr. Yu got married.

657
00:42:42,293 --> 00:42:43,928
How girlish.

658
00:42:44,595 --> 00:42:46,497
Dear Mr. Yu.

659
00:42:50,534 --> 00:42:53,904
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

660
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:58,208
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

661
00:42:58,709 --> 00:43:03,380
<i>Despising the herd mentality,</i>
<i>authority and institutional restraints...</i>

662
00:43:04,181 --> 00:43:07,217
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>

663
00:43:07,751 --> 00:43:09,119
<i>and the skills she has earned.</i>

664
00:43:12,389 --> 00:43:15,359
Hello? Akira? I'm heading there now.

665
00:43:15,559 --> 00:43:17,494
Michiko, you're late.

666
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:18,896
I'm almost done eating.

667
00:43:19,163 --> 00:43:20,798
Thank you for waiting.
Where would you like the meat?

668
00:43:20,864 --> 00:43:22,866
Put it here.

669
00:43:23,133 --> 00:43:24,568
Where are you?

670
00:43:24,835 --> 00:43:26,737
Hold on, let me look at the map.

671
00:43:31,575 --> 00:43:32,409
I'm in the fourth district.

672
00:43:32,643 --> 00:43:34,979
I'm in the second district.

673
00:43:35,346 --> 00:43:36,947
Where are you going?

674
00:43:37,181 --> 00:43:39,683
This map says...

675
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:42,286
You're just a woman
who can't read maps.

676
00:43:42,519 --> 00:43:44,989
If you don't get here, there isn't
going to be any more meat.

677
00:43:45,322 --> 00:43:48,258
Wait! Wait!

678
00:43:48,359 --> 00:43:50,594
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

679
00:43:51,161 --> 00:43:54,064
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

680
00:43:54,131 --> 00:43:56,834
Hold on! Wait!

681
00:45:14,311 --> 00:45:16,680
A patient is transferred here
from Keirin University Hospital?

682
00:45:16,814 --> 00:45:19,950
It is unthinkable that a Keirin
Hospital member is coming here.

683
00:45:20,050 --> 00:45:21,185
A gang leader?

684
00:45:21,285 --> 00:45:22,553
What did you say?

685
00:45:22,653 --> 00:45:25,055
They're here to tarnish
our reputation.

686
00:45:25,122 --> 00:45:26,790
How about you
die somewhere else?

687
00:45:26,890 --> 00:45:28,792
There is nothing
more important than life!
